# Squash solo - Ladder: Ball Behind You
@description Hitting straight when the ball has got past you, in sixteen levels on the forehand and
  backhand: from shadow swings in the stance, to balls dropped behind you, to moving back from the
  T. Based on AR Proformance and Squash Originals.
@speech rate 1.1
@minimum gap 0:00.8
@workout squash
@artwork ../images/squash.jpg
@include ../shared/squash.overtone

## Intro
Back corner ladder: hitting straight when the ball has got past you. Each level is played on the
forehand in the back right, then the backhand in the back left. Play the chapter for your level and
repeat it until you reach the target, then move on to the next. After a miss, count from zero.

// Hitting straight from a ball that has got past you, from AR Proformance ("Do This To Hit The Ball When
// It's Behind You": the stance, then soft high shots to the back of the service box) and Squash
// Originals (going with the ball, dropping the racket head). Each level moves the ball further behind
// the player, then adds the move to it. Each level is written out for both sides, as the stance differs.
## Level 1A: Forehand, the stance, no ball
@ladder
Forehand, the stance, no ball. In the back right corner, halfway between the service box and the
back wall, a racket and an arm off the side wall. Without a ball, set up in an open stance: face the
back corner, right foot nearest the back wall and last to land, left heel up so your hips can turn.
Racket set right back. Swing slowly: drop the racket head below the ball, swing up through it, and
finish straight down the wall.
+0:00.7 Target: ten slow swings, every one with the feet, chest and finish right.
+0:00.7 Open stance, facing the corner. Left heel up.
+0:00.7 Finish down the wall, not into the middle.

## Level 1B: Backhand, the stance, no ball
@ladder
Backhand, the stance, no ball. In the back left corner, halfway between the service box and the back
wall, a racket and an arm off the side wall. Without a ball, set up in a closed stance: back turned
toward the front wall, right foot stepping across toward the back corner and last to land, left heel
up so your hips can turn. Racket set right back. Swing slowly: drop the racket head below the ball,
swing up through it, and finish straight down the wall.
+0:00.7 Target: ten slow swings, every one with the feet, chest and finish right.
+0:00.7 Closed stance, right foot across. Left heel up.
+0:00.7 Finish down the wall, not into the middle.

## Level 2A: Forehand, from a drop
@ladder
Forehand, from a drop. At the back of the right service box, a racket and an arm off the side wall.
Set up in the stance, drop the ball a racket's length out toward the side wall, level with your
right foot, let it bounce, and hit it soft and high straight down the wall, first bounce near the
back of the service box. Catch it, set up again, and drop the next one.
+0:00.7 Target: five without a break, each bouncing first near the back of the service box.
+0:00.7 Soft and high. Height gets it deep.
+0:00.7 Racket head below the ball, then up through it.

## Level 2B: Backhand, from a drop
@ladder
Backhand, from a drop. At the back of the left service box, a racket and an arm off the side wall.
Set up in the stance, drop the ball a racket's length out toward the side wall, level with your
right foot, let it bounce, and hit it soft and high straight down the wall, first bounce near the
back of the service box. Catch it, set up again, and drop the next one.
+0:00.7 Target: five without a break, each bouncing first near the back of the service box.
+0:00.7 Soft and high. Height gets it deep.
+0:00.7 Racket head below the ball, then up through it.

## Level 3A: Forehand, deeper
@ladder
Forehand, deeper. Move back, halfway between the service box and the back wall. Same stance, now
with the ball dropped level with your right heel, further toward the back wall. Turn well, so the
racket has room and doesn't catch the wall.
+0:00.7 Target: seven out of ten, straight, bouncing first behind the short line.
+0:00.7 Lower ball? Bend your knees, don't bend over.
+0:00.7 Balanced through the swing.

## Level 3B: Backhand, deeper
@ladder
Backhand, deeper. Move back, halfway between the service box and the back wall. Same stance, now
with the ball dropped level with your right heel, further toward the back wall. Turn well, so the
racket has room and doesn't catch the wall.
+0:00.7 Target: seven out of ten, straight, bouncing first behind the short line.
+0:00.7 Lower ball? Bend your knees, don't bend over.
+0:00.7 Balanced through the swing.

## Level 4A: Forehand, off the side wall
@ladder
Forehand, off the side wall. At the back of the right service box. Throw the ball against the side
wall, a metre from the back wall, so it bounces behind you. Move back with it, alongside the box,
not across into the ball, set up facing the corner, and play it straight and high.
+0:00.7 Target: seven out of ten, straight, bouncing first behind the short line.
+0:00.7 Go with the ball, not at it.
+0:00.7 Open stance, facing the corner.

## Level 4B: Backhand, off the side wall
@ladder
Backhand, off the side wall. At the back of the left service box. Throw the ball against the side
wall, a metre from the back wall, so it bounces behind you. Move back with it, alongside the box,
not across into the ball, set up facing the corner, and play it straight and high.
+0:00.7 Target: seven out of ten, straight, bouncing first behind the short line.
+0:00.7 Go with the ball, not at it.
+0:00.7 Closed stance, right foot across.

## Level 5A: Forehand, past you
@ladder
Forehand, past you. Just behind the short line on the right. Hit yourself a high, soft straight
drive that bounces behind the service box and goes past you. Shuffle back alongside it, set up
facing the corner, and play it straight and high. Collect it, and go again.
+0:00.7 Target: seven out of ten, straight, bouncing first behind the short line.
+0:00.7 First step a shuffle. Keep the court in view.
+0:00.7 Quick off the mark, then slow into the shot.

## Level 5B: Backhand, past you
@ladder
Backhand, past you. Just behind the short line on the left. Hit yourself a high, soft straight drive
that bounces behind the service box and goes past you. Shuffle back alongside it, set up facing the
corner, and play it straight and high. Collect it, and go again.
+0:00.7 Target: seven out of ten, straight, bouncing first behind the short line.
+0:00.7 First step a shuffle. Keep the court in view.
+0:00.7 Quick off the mark, then slow into the shot.

## Level 6A: Forehand, step in or turn
@ladder
Forehand, step in or turn. Just behind the short line on the right. Feed yourself straight drives
without choosing their length, so some sit up in the box and some go past you. Short of you, get
behind it and step in. Past you, turn and face the corner. Either way, play it straight.
+0:00.7 Target: ten in the right stance, seven of them bouncing first behind the short line.
+0:00.7 Easy ball? Step in. Beaten? Turn.
+0:00.7 Decide as it bounces.

## Level 6B: Backhand, step in or turn
@ladder
Backhand, step in or turn. Just behind the short line on the left. Feed yourself straight drives
without choosing their length, so some sit up in the box and some go past you. Short of you, get
behind it and step in. Past you, turn and face the corner. Either way, play it straight.
+0:00.7 Target: ten in the right stance, seven of them bouncing first behind the short line.
+0:00.7 Easy ball? Step in. Beaten? Turn.
+0:00.7 Decide as it bounces.

## Level 7A: Forehand, from the T
@ladder
Forehand, from the T. Start on the T. Hit a high, soft forehand onto the front wall, right of
centre, so it goes deep down the right wall. Split step, move back with it, play it straight and
high from the corner, then push back to the T and go again.
+0:00.7 Target: seven out of ten, back to the T after every one.
+0:00.7 Push off your right foot, back to the T.
+0:00.7 Hips to the front on the way back, chest turned.

## Level 7B: Backhand, from the T
@ladder
Backhand, from the T. Start on the T. Hit a high, soft backhand onto the front wall, left of centre,
so it goes deep down the left wall. Split step, move back with it, play it straight and high from
the corner, then push back to the T and go again.
+0:00.7 Target: seven out of ten, back to the T after every one.
+0:00.7 Push off your right foot, back to the T.
+0:00.7 Hips to the front on the way back, chest turned.

## Level 8A: Forehand, kept going
@ladder
Forehand, kept going. At the back of the right service box. Straight forehand drives, kept going,
standing deep so each ball gets past you before you play it. Every one in the stance, facing the
corner, high and soft enough to come back to you.
+0:00.7 Target: ten without a break.
+0:00.7 Higher and softer to keep it going.
+0:00.7 Same stance every time.

## Level 8B: Backhand, kept going
@ladder
Backhand, kept going. At the back of the left service box. Straight backhand drives, kept going,
standing deep so each ball gets past you before you play it. Every one in the stance, facing the
corner, high and soft enough to come back to you.
+0:00.7 Target: ten without a break.
+0:00.7 Higher and softer to keep it going.
+0:00.7 Same stance every time.
